{{smaller block|In the ''water-carriage'' system each house has its own network of drain-pipes, soil-pipes, and waste-pipes, which lead from the basins, sinks, closets, and gullies within and about the house to the common sewer. ''Encyc. Brit.'', XXI. 714.}}
